meta { name: Refusal — published slug is locked, type: http, seq: 5 }

patch { url: {{adminBase}}/articles/{{articleId}}, body: json, auth: none }

headers { Cookie: {{sessionCookie}} }

body:json {
  {
    "slug": "a-completely-different-slug"
  }
}

docs {
  Against a PUBLISHED article. Expect 409 ARTICLE_SLUG_LOCKED.

  The slug is a live public URL: already shared, indexed by crawlers, and cached
  in ISR pages that only revalidate on publish. Changing it breaks every one of
  those silently, so the aggregate refuses. Unpublish first if it really must
  change.

  The same request against a DRAFT succeeds.
}
